{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_014toLXrS7BvU7BxtgNejXSe", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.03028\"}, {\"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1302.2898\"}, {\"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2003.06458\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bnaskrecki.faculty.wmi.amu.edu.pl/vietnam2026/book/peano/kernel.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.cs.ru.nl/~freek/factor/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://git.softlab.ece.ntua.gr/research/cpdt/commit/36799da7b831ec95d1669d1c97f89d452f84335c?w=1\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.cs.ru.nl/~freek/factor/factor.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://cljdoc.org/d/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/1.0b7-SNAPSHOT\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bnaskrecki.faculty.wmi.amu.edu.pl/vietnam2026/slides/lecture6.html\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:06:25.642Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "de Bruijn criterion Automath small kernel", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_012K4E7yHP2LdLzebqJZhpea", "content": [{"title": "A Survey on Theorem Provers in Formal Methods", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.03028"}, {"title": "Mathematics in the Age of the Turing Machine", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1302.2898"}, {"title": "QED at Large: A Survey of Engineering of Formally Verified Software", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2003.06458"}, {"title": "The kernel and the De Bruijn criterion#", "url": "https://bnaskrecki.faculty.wmi.amu.edu.pl/vietnam2026/book/peano/kernel.html"}, {"title": "The \"de Bruijn factor\"", "url": "https://www.cs.ru.nl/~freek/factor/"}, {"title": "git.softlab.ece.ntua.gr", "url": "https://git.softlab.ece.ntua.gr/research/cpdt/commit/36799da7b831ec95d1669d1c97f89d452f84335c?w=1"}, {"title": "www.cs.ru.nl", "url": "https://www.cs.ru.nl/~freek/factor/factor.pdf"}, {"title": "The (very) small kernel of the LaTTe proof assistant in Clojure(script)", "url": "https://cljdoc.org/d/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/1.0b7-SNAPSHOT"}, {"title": "VIASM Mini-Course · Hanoi 2026 · Lecture 6", "url": "https://bnaskrecki.faculty.wmi.amu.edu.pl/vietnam2026/slides/lecture6.html"}]}, "The results define the de Bruijn criterion but say little about Automath's kernel specifically.\n\n- **The criterion:** A proof assistant satisfies it when it produces proof objects that a small checking kernel can verify. It requires that they produce proof objects that a small proof-checking kernel can verify. Coq, Isabelle/HOL, HOL Light, and Agda are commonly cited as examples.\n- **Why it matters:** Search and tactic code can be buggy without invalidating a result, because only the final proof term needs checking. One source notes that one can ignore the possibility of bugs during search and rely on a relatively small proof-checking kernel applied to the result of the search.\n- **Size example:** HOL Light's kernel is a commonly cited example, at just 430 lines of very readable computer code. A survey gives a different figure, several hundred lines of OCaml.\n- **Automath link:** The results show that de Bruijn wrote about Automath, the system the criterion is named after. In his survey of Automath, he described a loss factor that stays roughly constant as a formalization proceeds. That is the \"de Bruijn factor,\" the ratio of formalized size to informal size. The results do not state how Automath's own checking was structured or how small its kernel was.\n\nThe sources don't confirm Automath's kernel size or design. If you need that, a search on Automath's checking architecture or de Bruijn's own papers would be the next step."], "durationSeconds": 8.036400375, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_014toLXrS7BvU7BxtgNejXSe", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDYDoQ6x9FgE8VDYxeNy", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "答案是**尼古拉斯·霍弗特·德布鲁因（Nicolaas Govert de Bruijn）**。\n\n他开发了 Automath。“只需信任一个小的证明检查内核”这条准则就以他的名字命名，叫“德布鲁因准则”（de Bruijn criterion）。\n\n我只搜了 1 次。搜到的网页说明了这条准则，也提到德布鲁因写过 Automath。他的全名和荷兰国籍是我自己的知识，网页里没有。\n\n来源：\n- [The kernel and the De Bruijn criterion](https://bnaskrecki.faculty.wmi.amu.edu.pl/vietnam2026/book/peano/kernel.html)\n- [The \"de Bruijn factor\"](https://www.cs.ru.nl/~freek/factor/)\n- [A Survey on Theorem Provers in Formal Methods](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.03028)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1229, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4295, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1229}, "output_tokens": 321, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:06:29.628Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDYDo8yVcCupoQSzocqB"}
